Applause!

Even the "well educated" ones are discouraged from critical examination 
of what "rewards" are worth striving for.

An education can be had by volunteering in a hospice and listening to the 
regrets of the dying. Conspicuously absent are statements like "I wish I 
had made more money."

One of my grad school professors used to make a point of saying to every 
class of teachers-to-be, "The only reason to send kids to school is to 
teach them their place." If it weren't so sad it would have been funny to 
see those thirty pairs of eyes glaze over.

